{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaZD9j9uVR7h68ym1SAE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Fix:** commit `e7052745` (PR #6145, TRUNK-6646), \"Env-var key normalization drops create_database_* / create_user_* credentials in scripted setup.\" Falkon's commit search matched the ticket key in the message, and I confirmed the change by reading its diff.\n\n**Cause:** `normalizeEnvVariableKey` lowercases each environment variable name and turns underscores into dots, unless the name is in `NON_NORMALIZED_KEYS`. `CREATE_DATABASE_USERNAME` therefore became `create.database.username`, which the installer never reads. The database user and password were dropped, so setup fell back to root with no password.\n\n**What the fix does:**\n- It adds `CREATE_DATABASE_USERNAME`, `CREATE_DATABASE_PASSWORD`, `CREATE_USER_USERNAME` and `CREATE_USER_PASSWORD` to the whitelist, so they keep their underscores. It also whitelists `CONNECTION_DRIVER_CLASS`, `IMPORT_TEST_DATA`, `REMOTE_URL`, `REMOTE_USERNAME`, `REMOTE_PASSWORD` and `ADMIN_PASSWORD_LOCKED`.\n- In `initializeWizardFromResolvedPropertiesIfPresent`, the driver class is also read from the `connection_driver_class` key. `import_test_data` (or `add_demo_data`) sets `importTestData`, and the remote URL and credentials are read from the script. The `admin.password.locked` property is stored under its dotted name.\n- The \"import test data\" path adds the `IMPORT_TEST_DATA` and `ADD_MODULES` wizard tasks.\n- Two new test classes cover the change: `InitializationFilterNormalizationTest` and new cases in `InitializationFilterTest`.\n\n**Code locations (post-fix, from the commit):**\n- `InitializationFilter.java` lines 197–200 hold the expanded whitelist. The `NON_NORMALIZED_KEYS` declaration runs to line 202.\n- `InitializationFilter.java` lines 1948–1953 hold `normalizeEnvVariableKey`, which checks the whitelist.\n- `InitializationFilter.java` lines 356–363 read `connection_driver_class` and the other script keys.\n- `InitializationFilter.java` lines 397–423 read the import-test-data, remote and admin-lock properties.\n- `InitializationFilter.java` lines 961–970 add the test-data tasks.\n- `InitializationFilterNormalizationTest.java` (new, lines 1–93) tests the normalization.\n- `InitializationFilterTest.java` gains two tests added by the commit. I did not read their line numbers.\n\nI did not verify the line numbers for lines 356–423 and 961–970 by reading the file. They come from the hunk headers in the diff, which give new-file positions.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-core\", \"commit\": \"e7052745fb78802c8adcd7c1962f3525e7050b1e\"},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-core\", \"pr\": 6145},\n  {\"ticket\": \"TRUNK-6646\"},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-core/web/src/main/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilter.java\", \"startLine\": 197, \"endLine\": 200},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-core/web/src/main/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilter.java\", \"startLine\": 1948, \"endLine\": 1953},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-core/web/src/main/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilter.java\", \"startLine\": 356, \"endLine\": 363},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-core/web/src/main/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilter.java\", \"startLine\": 397, \"endLine\": 423},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-core/web/src/main/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilter.java\", \"startLine\": 961, \"endLine\": 970},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-core/web/src/test/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilterNormalizationTest.java\", \"startLine\": 1, \"endLine\": 93}\n]\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2288,"cache_read_input_tokens":28587,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2288},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a3107f6-99d9-4a89-8e9a-236990805063","uuid":"aa955e13-ebc6-4ffa-ab83-9489ddd29273","timestamp":"2026-10-31T15:32:04.542Z","request_id":"req_011CgaZD9RYLzTB7pTbPEvZX"}
